/-!
# Set (d), master `I₁₃`: the parts of `Ψ₄'` and `p₄` in the Lyndon basis

Each part of the check `Ψ₄'(ξ) ξ'(t) = p₄(t)` is written as a polynomial in `ξ`, `log ξ` and the
Lyndon basis functions `H(l; ξ)` (`QED.ThreeLoopD.i13hw_m0` and its companions): the parts
`Nⱼ` of `Ψ₄` (`QED.ThreeLoopD.i13Psi4N0_eq`, …), the derivatives of the parts multiplied by
`ξ (1 - ξ) (1 + ξ)` to clear the kernels (`QED.ThreeLoopD.i13Psi4dN0a_eq`, …), and `ξ p₄`
(`QED.ThreeLoopD.i13P4x_eq`). The polynomials (`QED.ThreeLoopD.i13Q4E0`, …) were generated by a
script.

## Main results

* `QED.ThreeLoopD.i13Psi4N0_eq`, `QED.ThreeLoopD.i13Psi4dN0a_eq`, `QED.ThreeLoopD.i13P4x_eq`.
-/

@[expose] public section

open Set Real QED.Polylog QED.Polylog.HPL QED.Polylog.HPL.Letter

namespace QED.ThreeLoopD

